# Round 18, C1-25 (follows). L §7.1: in rules the only figures are 0, 1, -1 and the rest of its list; "Every other
# figure ... is a row" (LOAD-LITERAL "figure <n> in a rule; make it a row"). A rule a version brings is a rule: §5.3's
# example is now `replace rule relief.disabled = disabled_relief when disabled[p]`.
=== m.tally
model m
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
input base_relief: money PLN
input disabled: bool
def relief: money PLN at reader
  rule base = base_relief
  rule disabled beats base = base_relief when disabled
version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-12-01
  base_relief = 1000
  disabled = true
version v2
  cite s
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-01-01
  replace rule relief.disabled = 1 500.00 PLN when disabled
ask q: relief law 2026-06-01
=== expect
refused: LOAD-LITERAL figure 1 500.00 PLN in a rule; make it a row (m.tally:23)
